      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the woman in the meme",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the woman depicted in the bottom panel of the meme. The meme's text 'lol she thinks she's a goat' implies the user is mocking or identifying with the perspective of someone who sees the woman as foolish or arrogant. The projection is onto the visual material of the woman, as the user is not explicitly deictic (e.g., 'me' or 'you'), but the humor and judgment are directed at the woman, making her the target of the user's implied projection. The user is projecting their own judgment or amusement onto the woman's perceived foolishness.",
